<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziying</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/206-bce">206 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Ziying of Qin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziying was the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a>. Placed on the throne in 207 BCE by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> Zhao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> after the Second Emperor's death, he had Zhao Gao killed and took the title King of Qin rather than emperor. After 46 days he surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianyang">Xianyang</a>, and weeks later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> occupied the city and put him to death.</p></div>
